 "analysis_en": [
  "At 11:30 on Friday, Nov 20, SJC bars were bid 129.2 and offered 134.2 million VND per tael, SJC rings 128–134 million. Versus the previous H79 board (Nov 17: bars 134.7–137.7, rings 133.5–137.5), both are down 5.5 million on the bid and 3.5 million on the ask. Versus the Nov 19 close (133.2–136.2), SJC bars are down 4 million bid and 2 million ask.",
  "Bid–ask spreads widened: 5 million on SJC bars (from 3 million) and 6 million on SJC rings. PNJ 24K rings are 127.8–132 million, down 5.2 million on both sides from Nov 17 (133–137.2); BTMC rings 128.6–133.6 million (Nov 17: 133.5–137.5).",
  "World gold is about $3,528.6/oz (CNBC XAU= $3,522.9 at 11:37), roughly 109.5 million VND per tael before taxes and fees. The SJC ask sits about 24.7 million above that (SJC rings about 24.5 million), far wider than about 17.6 million on Nov 17 – world prices fell faster than local ones.",
  "Anyone who bought at the 191.3 million peak (Jan 29, 2026) and sold back today at the 129.2 million bid would lose about 62.1 million VND per tael (≈ 32.5%)."
 ],
 "advice_en": "World gold has broken well below the old 3,700–3,600 plan zone and sits at a 14-month low: a December Fed hike is almost fully priced (CME FedWatch ~96%), the dollar is near a 19-month high and the 10-year yield is above 5%.\nPhysical buyers: don't catch a falling knife. If you buy, split it into small portions.\nNext reference zone is $3,500: about 108.6 million VND per tael (3,500 × 25,730 VND/USD × 1.20565, before taxes and fees). With today's 24.7 million premium, SJC bars would be around 133.3 million; if the premium shrinks back to about 17.6 million as on Nov 17, around 126.2 million.\nThe ~24.7 million premium is unusually wide: local prices may lag a world rebound, and if the premium narrows SJC can fall further even with world gold flat.\nIf you bought at the peak: don't panic-sell into the drop; only add with idle money.",
